course: dictionary
lesson: 352
title: What an antacid does
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An antacid is a medicine that makes stomach acid weaker. Look at the word in two parts: anti means against, and acid is the sour liquid in your stomach. So an antacid works against acid.
explain: «Dad takes an antacid tablet for heartburn.» Heartburn is a burning feeling, and the tablet helps it ease. Antacids are used after spicy or big meals, but only when an adult or doctor says it is safe.
explain: The alkali in an antacid «cancels some stomach acid». An alkali is a base, and when it meets an acid the two react and the acid becomes less acidic. Scientists call this neutralisation.
fact: An antacid is a medicine that makes stomach acid weaker.
fact: «Antacid» can also be an adjective, as in «antacid tablets», meaning tablets that work against acid.
fact: Many antacids contain calcium carbonate or magnesium hydroxide.
fact: In neutralisation, an alkali reacts with an acid and makes it less acidic.
fact: Medicines, including antacids, are only taken with an adult's permission or as a doctor directs.
exercise: «Dad takes an antacid tablet for heartburn.» What is an antacid? | A machine that measures heat | A food that adds more acid to your stomach | A sweet, sour snack for your lunchbox | *A medicine that makes stomach acid weaker
exercise: In «antacid tablets», what kind of word is antacid? | *An adjective, describing the tablets | An adverb, describing how you swallow | A noun, the name of a thing | A verb, an action word
exercise: What does the alkali in an antacid do to stomach acid? | It turns the acid into sugar | It makes the acid stronger | *It cancels some of the acid, so it is less acidic | It has no effect at all
test: Which two ingredients may an antacid contain? | Vitamin C and iron | Sugar and salt | Oil and vinegar | *Calcium carbonate and magnesium hydroxide
test: What should you do before taking any antacid? | *Ask an adult or doctor for permission | Take two tablets to be safe | Eat a big meal first | Share it with a friend who has a sore tummy
exam: «Antacid tablets contain an alkali that cancels some stomach acid.» In science, what is this process called? | *Neutralisation | Condensation | Photosynthesis | Evaporation
